<BaseLayout title="Ecosystem" description="How PlayMAKER's web, tagging and video tools are intended to exchange data as development progresses." path="/ecosystem/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">The ecosystem</p><h1>One club.<br />Many ways to play.</h1><p class="section-lede">The tools are modular. Connections between them are being designed, and the full workflow is not yet available.</p></div></section>
  <section class="page-section"><div class="shell"><div class="content-grid"><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">01 / Publish</p><h2>WebMAKER</h2><p>Start with a static club site for identity, news, matches and statistics. A pilot is being beta tested with Nerone Basket Anzio.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">02 / Capture</p><h2>TagMAKER</h2><p>Tag moments in match video and export structured event data. Profiles and export formats are planned for the MVP; no stable schema is published yet.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">03 / Create</p><h2>VideoMAKER</h2><p>Turn full-game footage into highlights. Import of TagMAKER data is planned, while editing and export remain in early development.</p></div><div class="panel"><p class="section-kicker">Interoperability</p><h2>Data should travel</h2><p>The goal is reusable match data. Exact import/export formats, compatibility versions and migration guidance will be published alongside working releases.</p></div></div><div class="callout"><p><strong>Current compatibility:</strong> No end-to-end WebMAKER → TagMAKER → VideoMAKER integration is released. Treat the diagrams and descriptions as roadmap, not a compatibility guarantee.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
